WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.707
Freshness is easiest to understand with a timeline.

00:00:03.707 --> 00:00:08.342
Imagine the materialized view is refreshed at nine in the morning.

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:13.062
At ten, a new admission is inserted into the source table.

00:00:13.062 --> 00:00:18.117
A normal query against the source can see that new row immediately.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:25.075
The materialized view cannot see it yet because its stored snapshot still represents nine o'clock.

00:00:25.889 --> 00:00:31.041
After the materialized view is refreshed again, the snapshot catches up.

00:00:31.041 --> 00:00:36.871
That time difference between the source and the snapshot is not automatically a problem.

00:00:36.871 --> 00:00:43.292
It becomes a problem only when users expect fresher data than the system is designed to provide.
